WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.095
Lottie couldn't understand why Sara didn't wear pretty dresses anymore.

2
00:00:17.096 --> 00:00:20.107
Or why Sara had to work now.

3
00:00:20.108 --> 00:00:24.126
"There's a new girl in your room," Lottie said to Sara.

4
00:00:24.127 --> 00:00:26.130
"Where do you sleep?"

5
00:00:26.131 --> 00:00:30.216
"Don't worry. I have a room," said Sara.

6
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:33.576
But she wouldn't tell Lottie where it was.

7
00:00:33.577 --> 00:00:37.186
Lottie was determined to find out.

8
00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:41.700
She listened to the older girls talking, and then she knew.

9
00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:48.678
Late one afternoon she climbed the stairs to the attic. She opened a door.

10
00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:53.145
There was Sara, standing on a table and looking out the skylight.

11
00:00:53.146 --> 00:00:58.654
"Sara!" Lottie looked horrified at the bare and empty attic.

12
00:00:58.655 --> 00:01:01.626
"This room is so ugly!"

13
00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:08.342
"Shh, Lottie!" Sara said quickly. "Don't cry or make any noise.

14
00:01:08.343 --> 00:01:13.224
You'll get us both in trouble. This isn't such a bad room."

15
00:01:13.225 --> 00:01:20.171
Lottie bit her lip as she looked around again. "Why not, Sara?"

16
00:01:20.172 --> 00:01:25.608
Sara hugged Lottie and forced herself to smile even though it had been a hard day.

17
00:01:25.609 --> 00:01:30.978
Then she helped Lottie to climb on top of the table so they could look out the skylight.

18
00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:35.937
"You can see all sorts of things from here," said Sara.

19
00:01:35.938 --> 00:01:38.956
"Things that you can't see from downstairs.

20
00:01:38.957 --> 00:01:43.359
I wish someone lived in the house next door, but it's empty.

21
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.806
If a person looked out the skylight in that house, we could talk."

22
00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:53.454
Two sparrows twittered and hopped about on the roof.

23
00:01:53.455 --> 00:01:56.781
"I see birds!" exclaimed Lottie.

24
00:01:56.782 --> 00:02:00.231
"I wish we could feed them," said Sara.

25
00:02:00.232 --> 00:02:03.703
"I have a bun from lunch!" Lottie shrieked.

26
00:02:03.704 --> 00:02:06.382
She pulled a bun from her pocket.

27
00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:11.831
The two girls broke the bun into pieces and fed the birds.

28
00:02:11.832 --> 00:02:18.449
"Oh, I like it here!" said Lottie. "It's much nicer than downstairs."

29
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:27.032
Sara nodded. "It's so little, and high above everything, it's like a nest in a tree," she said.

30
00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:31.118
"In the morning I can lie in bed and look right up at the sky.

31
00:02:31.119 --> 00:02:35.786
And if there are stars at night, I can lie here and count them."

32
00:02:35.787 --> 00:02:40.877
"I'd like to live here too!" Lottie declared.

33
00:02:40.878 --> 00:02:44.312
Sara laughed. "It's time for you to go, Lottie.

34
00:02:44.313 --> 00:02:48.808
I don't want anyone to find you here."

35
00:02:48.809 --> 00:02:54.546
Sara helped Lottie off the table and out the door.

36
00:02:54.547 --> 00:02:57.958
Then she sat and looked around the room.

37
00:02:57.959 --> 00:03:02.602
Without Lottie, it was much harder to pretend her room was nice.

38
00:03:02.603 --> 00:03:06.329
The bed was hard and covered with a dingy blanket.

39
00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:12.772
The floor was cold and bare, and the footstool with the injured leg was the only seat in the room.

40
00:03:12.773 --> 00:03:18.266
"Sometimes this is the loneliest place in the world," she said.

41
00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:21.751
Just then she heard a little noise.

42
00:03:21.752 --> 00:03:26.488
A large rat stood quite close to her, sniffing the air.

43
00:03:26.489 --> 00:03:31.415
Another child might have jumped back, but Sara stayed still.

44
00:03:31.416 --> 00:03:36.703
The rat could smell some crumbs that Lottie had dropped.

45
00:03:36.704 --> 00:03:43.371
The rat looked odd and strange, like a gnome with gray whiskers.

46
00:03:43.372 --> 00:03:47.400
"I won't hurt you," Sara said quietly.

47
00:03:47.401 --> 00:03:54.533
"Prisoners in the Bastille made friends with rats. I could be your friend."

48
00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:58.469
The rat came closer and ate a small crumb.

49
00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:04.014
Then he snatched a bigger crumb and ran into his hole.

50
00:04:04.015 --> 00:04:06.772
"He probably took that home to his family!"

51
00:04:06.773 --> 00:04:13.805
Sara was delighted with her new friend. "I think I'll call him Mel."

52
00:04:13.806 --> 00:04:20.547
Over the next week Mel gradually grew to trust Sara.

53
00:04:20.548 --> 00:04:24.112
She gave him food and never frightened him.

54
00:04:24.113 --> 00:04:28.866
One night Ermengarde came to visit.

55
00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:32.612
She sat on Sara's bed while Sara sat on the footstool.

56
00:04:32.613 --> 00:04:35.926
"I have a new friend," said Sara.

57
00:04:35.927 --> 00:04:41.016
"But you must promise not to be frightened by him. He's a rat."

58
00:04:41.017 --> 00:04:46.239
"A rat!" Ermengarde cried and pulled her shawl tightly around her.

59
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:55.002
"He's very nice," Sara went on. "I call him Mel. Watch this, Ermengarde."

60
00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:59.994
Sara gave a low whistle, and Mel came out of his hole.

61
00:04:59.995 --> 00:05:06.309
She dropped some crumbs on the floor. Mel gobbled them up.

62
00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:11.209
"He always saves a few for his wife and children," said Sara.

63
00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:15.146
"They live in a cozy nest in the wall."

64
00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:19.658
Ermengarde was delighted by this story. "Tell me more."

65
00:05:19.659 --> 00:05:24.704
But before Sara could say anything, someone knocked twice on the wall.

66
00:05:24.705 --> 00:05:28.749
"What's that?" Ermengarde's eyes were wide with fear.

67
00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.973
"Just the prisoner in the next cell," Sara said.

68
00:05:32.974 --> 00:05:36.345
"Becky!" Ermengarde exclaimed.

69
00:05:36.346 --> 00:05:41.697
"Two knocks mean 'Are you there?'" Sara explained.

70
00:05:41.698 --> 00:05:44.445
Then she rapped three times on the wall.

71
00:05:44.446 --> 00:05:48.572
"And three knocks mean 'Yes, all is well.'"

72
00:05:48.573 --> 00:05:51.702
Becky knocked four times.

73
00:05:51.703 --> 00:05:56.358
"That means 'Good night. Sleep well,'" said Sara.

74
00:05:56.359 --> 00:06:00.741
Ermengarde beamed. "It's just like a story!"

75
00:06:00.742 --> 00:06:06.849
"Yes. You can be an escaped prisoner in the story," Sara told her.

76
00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:14.331
"But now it's time to sneak to your bed downstairs."
